# Two Dire Blunderbusses on one Ornithopter give it two instances of "Whenever this creature attacks, you may sacrifice an
# artifact other than Dire Blunderbuss ..." (CR 613.1f), each naming the Blunderbuss that grants it. Both trigger when
# it attacks. As the first resolves, its own Blunderbuss may not be sacrificed (the refusal) but the other may, and is
# (the positive control): the reflexive ability deals 3, the power the creature has with one Blunderbuss left, to Bot2's
# Ornithopter. As the second resolves, its own Blunderbuss is gone and the first one is now an artifact it may
# sacrifice: sacrificed, the reflexive ability deals the creature's power, now 0, to the one creature left.
# In the graveyard each is a Dire Flail again, its front face (CR 712.8a).
# Setup: the first Flail crafts on turn three with the Black Lotus card in the graveyard as its material; the second on
# turn seven with a second Ornithopter.

